## Why the GPL-3.0 dependency does not make this project GPL-3.0

`account-abstraction` is GPL-3.0 as a repository, but it licenses its files
individually and the ones on this project's deployment path are all MIT:

- `LaneAccount` inherits `contracts/accounts/Simple7702Account.sol` (MIT), which
  inherits `contracts/core/BaseAccount.sol` (MIT) and MIT interfaces.
- `contracts/core/EntryPoint.sol` is GPL-3.0. It is imported only by
  `test/ParallelNonce.t.sol`, so that it can be placed at the canonical address
  inside the Foundry test VM. It is never deployed or redistributed by this
  project: EntryPoint v0.8 already exists on Sei as a singleton at
  `0x4337084D9E255Ff0702461CF8895CE9E3b5Ff108`, and the application calls that
  deployment.

If you vendor or redistribute any part of `lib/account-abstraction` beyond the
MIT files listed above, review its terms yourself. This note describes how the
dependency is used here; it is not legal advice.
